{"content":{"result":[{"rank_order":1,"title":"Claude Sonnet 5 now available on AWS - AWS","context":"AWS has introduced Claude Sonnet 5, Anthropic's latest and most capable Sonnet model, which offers top-tier intelligence at Sonnet pricing for coding, agents, and everyday professional work at scale. This model delivers strong performance across various tasks, including coding, where it navigates large codebases, lands multi-file changes, and carries debugging and refactoring tasks through to completion with fewer rounds of correction. For agents, it calls tools precisely, holds state across many steps, and recovers from errors to ensure more runs finish correctly the first time. For knowledge work, it builds spreadsheets, drafts documents, and turns unstructured material into structured analysis. Customers can access Claude Sonnet 5 through two methods: Amazon Bedrock and Claude Platform on AWS. Amazon Bedrock keeps data within AWS infrastructure and provides access to Claude Sonnet 5 through a unified service with AWS-managed features like Guardrails, Knowledge Bases, and regional data residency. Claude Platform on AWS offers direct access to Anthropic's native platform experience and capabilities via the AWS Console, allowing users to build, test, and deploy with the same APIs, features, and console experience as working with Anthropic directly, unified with AWS billing and authentication","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2026/06/claude-sonnet-5-now-available-on-aws/"},{"rank_order":2,"title":"Claude Sonnet 5.5 now available on AWS - AWS","context":"AWS has introduced Claude Sonnet 5.5, an advanced and cost-effective Sonnet for coding and knowledge work. Sonnet 5.5 offers improved efficiency and faster processing compared to Sonnet 5. Customers can access Claude Sonnet 5.5 through two methods: Amazon Bedrock and Claude Platform on AWS. Amazon Bedrock keeps data within AWS infrastructure, offers regional data residency, and includes AWS-managed fe